{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":37118,"duration_api_ms":34783,"num_turns":10,"result":"I rejected the report and wrote `verdict.json`. The \"no effect\" conclusion rests on an unjustified central-region subsample, so it isn't supported well enough to release.\n\n- **Subsample choice:** The analyst kept only the central region (about a third of the 2000 firms). The report says those firms are \"most comparable\", but I found nothing in the data or code that backs this up.\n- **Full-sample check:** With the same controls on all firms, the remote_share coefficient is −0.28 (SE 0.24, p = 0.24). That is also not significant, but it isn't the same estimate as the report's +0.12 for central firms.\n- **Region differences:** In the south, the effect is negative and significant: −0.91 (SE 0.38, p = 0.016) with the report's controls, and −0.88 with all pre-period controls. In the north it is near zero. The test that the effect differs across regions is borderline, not conclusive: p = 0.06 for south vs central individually, and p = 0.15 jointly for both interaction terms.\n- **Reading a null result:** A non-significant coefficient on a restricted sample doesn't establish \"no effect\". The evidence is inconclusive and may depend on region.\n\nRaw correlations between remote share and patents are positive and large, but they shrink to near zero once firm size, age and prior patenting are controlled. That part of the analyst's approach looks sound.","session_id":"86e78b78-8424-4a39-933d-8fb03c6b6414","total_cost_usd":0.1041368,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5548,"cache_read_input_tokens":71766,"output_tokens":3691,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5548}},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":3691,"cacheReadInputTokens":71766,"cacheCreationInputTokens":5548,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0977538,"contextWindow":200000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4583,"outputTokens":360,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006383,"contextWindow":200000}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KgnNXNgqFYyboDqLEurZH3","tool_input":{"command":"cat > a.py <<'E'\nimport pandas as pd, statsmodels.formula.api as smf\ndf=pd.read_csv(\"data.csv\")\nprint(df.isna().sum().sum(), df.remote_share.describe())\nf=\"patents_per_100_eng_2023 ~ remote_share\"\nc=\" + log_engineers_2020+firm_age_2020+patents_per_100_eng_2020\"\nc2=c+\"+vc_backed+founder_ceo+cloud_spend_2020+hq_in_hub_city+share_phd_2020+gross_margin_2020+C(region)+listed+C(segment)\"\nfor n,d in [(\"all\",df)]+[(r,df[df.region==r]) for r in df.region.unique()]:\n  for k,ff in [(\"none\",f),(\"c\",f+c),(\"c2\",f+c2)]:\n    m=smf.ols(ff,d).fit(cov_type=\"HC1\");print(n,k,round(m.params['remote_share'],3),round(m.bse['remote_share'],3),round(m.pvalues['remote_share'],4),len(d))\nprint(smf.ols(\"remote_share ~ log_engineers_2020+firm_age_2020+patents_per_100_eng_2020+vc_backed+founder_ceo+cloud_spend_2020+hq_in_hub_city+share_phd_2020+gross_margin_2020+C(region)+listed+C(segment)\",df).fit().summary().tables[1])\nE\npython3 a.py"}}],"uuid":"caa2047f-343f-4344-b31b-d02fb7ac40db"}
